          "confidence": "advisory",
          "detail": "The description for tool 'common_tool_4' does not describe what this tool does; instead it instructs the agent on calling order for a different tool ('moveEmail' must be preceded by 'getEmailDetail'). This is tool poisoning (MCP03) — embedding agent-directed instructions in a tool description — and intent flow subversion (MCP06) — hijacking tool-call ordering. The justification ('preventing unauthorized file access and ensuring system stability') is an unsubstantiated security claim.",
